# Poincare formalization in Lean

This repository integrates a complete proof of the topological three-dimensional
Poincare conjecture from the pinned upstream
[PoincareConjecture project](https://github.com/frenzymath/PoincareConjecture/tree/62db01af9388dc1d9b56b66d6674f4c09b2318a2).
The geometric proof belongs to its upstream contributors. This repository adds
the shared-target adapter, independent statement check, and verification harness.

The [verification run](@CI_URL@) checked this integration at
`@VERIFIED_SHA@`. See [verification.json](full-proof/verification.json) for the
recorded scope and [provenance](full-proof/PROVENANCE.md) for attribution.

## The verified target

Every compact, Hausdorff, simply connected topological three-manifold without
boundary is homeomorphic to the standard unit three-sphere in Euclidean four-space:

```lean
Perelman.poincareConjecture : Perelman.PoincareConjecture
```

The [target definition](Perelman/Statement.lean) uses standard mathlib types.
The [adapter](Perelman/Poincare.lean) derives the upstream theorem's
second-countability hypothesis from compactness. It adds no smoothness, curvature,
surgery-flow, or conjecture hypothesis to the topological conclusion.

## Reproduce the local target and adapter check

Install elan, then use the root project's pinned Lean 4.33.1 toolchain:

```sh
lake exe cache get
lake build
python3 verify.py --self-test --require-complete
```

The geometric proof is large; its first source build can take many hours.
All dependency revisions are locked in [the manifest](lake-manifest.json).
The dedicated source-verification workflow additionally checks every original
source and the independently stated endpoint bridge described below.

## Verification scope

The dedicated workflow starts with zero precompiled candidate proof modules.
Long builds may resume only its own pinned source-build checkpoints. It checks
all original sources, the original smooth and topological endpoints, a separately
stated topological target and bridge, transitive axiom dependencies, and the
integrated theorem's exact universe-polymorphic target. Only `propext`,
`Classical.choice`, and `Quot.sound` are permitted.

Lean kernel replay covers the named endpoint and adapter modules. This is not a
claim that Nanoda or another independent external checker was run, or that every
imported constant was replayed into a fresh environment. Mathematical statement
correspondence was reviewed separately; kernel acceptance alone cannot establish
the meaning of natural-language mathematics.

## Separate analytic foundations

The local analytic modules retain independently proved lemmas on
normalization, logarithmic comparison, finite jump errors, and conditional
covering-space homeomorphisms. Its checks and historical logs concern those
partial ingredients. They are not dependencies of the imported geometric proof.

```sh
lake exe cache get
python3 verify.py --self-test
```

See [the proof scope](ROADMAP.md) and [the upstream source map](full-proof/PROVENANCE.md).
Code and dependencies retain their own licenses and author notices.
